---
title: Chicken Tostadas
servings: 6
prepTime: 45 min
cookTime: 40 min
Rating: 8/10
source: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/chicken-tostadas-recipe-2117736
tags: Chicken
---

= Chicken =
In a small bowl, mix together the @chicken{3%cups}(cooked and shredded), @lime juice{1/3%cup},
@olive oil{1/4%cup}, @cilantro{1/4%cup}(chopped), and @salt, and season with @pepper to taste.
Cover with plastic wrap and set aside.

= Tostadas =
In a saucepan, warm up @refried beans{15%oz}, using pre-canned beans or your favorite recipe.

Preheat the broiler.
Spread the beans evenly over one side of each @flat corn tortillas{6}
and sprinkle with some of the @Monterey Jack cheese{1/2%cup}(shredded).
Transfer to a baking sheet and broil until the cheese is lightly browned and melted, about 30 seconds.
Divide the tortillas among 6 plates.

= Serving Options =
Evenly mound the chicken on each tortilla and top with the @iceberg lettuce{2%cups}(cored and shredded).
Top each tostada with @?avocado{1}(thinly sliced or Guacamole), @?salsa cruda{2%cups}, and a dollop of @?sour cream{1/2%cup}.
Sprinkle with the @scallion{1}(thinly sliced) and garnish the tostada with the @?cilantro{12%leaves}. Serve immediately.
